<title>CANADA: Canada crushes 234,000 tonnes canola in March.</title>
<headline>Canada crushes 234,000 tonnes canola in March.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada said on Friday that oilseed processors crushed 234,160 metric tonnes of canola in March.</p>
<p>Oil production totaled 98,485 tonnes, while meal production was 141,457 tonnes, StatsCan said.</p>
<p>Between August 1996 and March 1997, processors crushed 1,810,396 metric tonnes.</p>
<p>This is the first time in the 1996-97 crop year that the cumulative canola crush was below that of the corresponding period in 1995-96. The August 1995 to March 1996 crush was 1,811,210 tonnes.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613 235-6745))</p>
</text>
